,"party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Robert Ray","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10531","person_slug":"robert-ray","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ross Lightfoot","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10389","person_slug":"ross-lightfoot","vote":"no"},{"name":"Russell Trood","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10640","person_slug":"russell-trood","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ruth Webber","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10662","person_slug":"ruth-webber","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sandy Macdonald","party":"Nationals","person_id":"tvfy_10402","person_slug":"sandy-macdonald","vote":"no"},{"name":"Simon Birmingham","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10044","person_slug":"simon-birmingham","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Fielding","party":"Family First","person_id":"tvfy_10221","person_slug":"steve-fielding","vote":"no"},{"name":"Steve Hutchins","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10323","person_slug":"steve-hutchins","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sue Boyce","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10062","person_slug":"sue-boyce","vote":"no"}],"name":"Great Barrier Reef Marine Park Amendment Bill 2007 - In Committee - Membership of GBRMPA","noes":33,"question":"The majority voted against a [motion](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?gid=2007-06-21.245.1) introduced by Australian Democrats Senator [Andrew Bartlett](http://publicwhip-rails.openaustraliafoundation.org.au/mp.php?mpn=Andrew_Bartlett&mpc=Senate&house=senate), which means it was unsuccessful. The motion was: _(1) Schedule 1, item 14, page 5 (line 8), omit paragraph 10(1)(b), substitute:_ _(b) a member appointed to represent the interests of the [Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_Australians) communities adjacent to the Marine Park;_ _(c) at least 1 but not more than 3 other members._ Senator Bartlett explained that the motion relates to the issue of the membership of the Great Barrier Reef Marine Park Authority (GBRMPA).(Read Senator Bartlett's full explanation and the associated debate [here](http://www.openaustralia.org/senate/?id=2007-06-21.244.1), starting from 6:58 pm. ) _Background to the bill_ The bill was introduced in response to recommendations made in the [Review of the Corporate Governance of Statutory Authorities and Office Holders](http://www.finance.gov.au/financial-framework/governance/review_corporate_governance.html) (the Uhrig Review).(Read more about the background to the bill in its [bills digest](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/bd/bd0607/07bd134). ) The bill amends the [Great Barrier Reef Marine Park Act 1975](http://www.austlii.edu.au/au/legis/cth/consol_act/gbrmpa1975257/) to: - implement changes to the governance arrangements of the [Great Barrier Reef Marine Park Authority](http://www.gbrmpa.gov.au/about-us); - provide for a periodic outlook report and the development of zoning plans for the Marine Park; and - replace the Great Barrier Reef Consultative Committee with a non-statutory advisory board.(A summary of the bill and its explanatory memorandum can be found [here](http://www.aph.gov.au/Parliamentary_Business/Bills_Legislation/Bills_Search_Results/Result?","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-1361","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2007-06-21/9"}
